# OnStandard — line-ending + diff rules.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-07-30). core.autocrlf is `true` on the founder's Windows box, so git
# rewrites line endings on checkout. assets/proto.zip is BUILT from the proto sources, so any
# checkout that flips a source file between LF and CRLF changes the bundle's bytes and its content
# hash (src/proto/protoVersion.ts) even though not one line of code changed.
#
# The symptom: `npm run preflight` regenerates the bundle, sees it differ from HEAD, and hard-stops
# on a dirty tree — right at ship time, with nothing actually wrong. The risk is worse than the
# annoyance: the obvious way out is to commit the "new" bundle, so the repo accumulates
# no-op bundle churn and a genuinely stale bundle stops being distinguishable from a line-ending
# one. (A stale bundle is how an OTA ships nothing — see the 2026-07-30 rebuild commit.)
#
# Marking the bundle binary stops git touching it. Marking the proto sources LF keeps what goes
# INTO the bundle byte-stable regardless of the platform it was built on, which is what makes the
# content hash mean "the proto changed" again.

# Never transform archives or images. They are not text and a CRLF pass would corrupt them.
*.zip     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.webp    binary
*.mp4     binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.p12     binary
*.p8      binary

# The bundled proto: byte-identical on every platform, so PROTO_VERSION only moves when the
# proto actually moves.
proto/redesign-2026-07/**/*.js   text eol=lf
proto/redesign-2026-07/**/*.mjs  text eol=lf
proto/redesign-2026-07/**/*.css  text eol=lf
proto/redesign-2026-07/**/*.html text eol=lf
proto/redesign-2026-07/**/*.json text eol=lf
proto/redesign-2026-07/**/*.md   text eol=lf
